From 1207b9379e14b32115c3067112e509d402dd0145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Lapin <a.lapin03@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:06:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): sign in through an authenticating reverse proxy

With T3CODE_PROXY_AUTH_SECRET set, the server trusts a reverse proxy that
has already signed the user in. The proxy sends the secret in the
X-T3code-Proxy-Auth header with every request. The first session check
from a browser that carries it gets a normal browser session cookie with
full access, so the app opens without a pairing link.

Requests without the secret get 401, so a published container port does
not bypass the proxy. Requests that bring their own bearer or DPoP token
and no cookie still pass, which keeps the CLI and agent MCP calls inside
the container working. The server does not print a pairing URL in this
mode. Without the variable nothing changes.
